---
import { relay } from '../../data/site';

const signInUrl = relay.signInUrl;
const earlyAccessHref = relay.signupUrl;
---

<header class="section_header26 products-hero">
  <div class="padding-global">
    <div class="header142_component">
      <div class="padding-global">
        <div class="container-large">
          <div class="padding-section-large">
            <div class="text-align-center">
              <div class="header142_content">
                <p class="heading-style-h6 products-eyebrow">Limited early access for Miri customers.</p>
                <div class="margin-bottom margin-small">
                  <h1 class="heading-style-h1 hero">Introducing Miri Relay</h1>
                </div>
                <p class="text-size-medium hero">Advanced SMS service notification for Aspire</p>
                <p class="text-size-medium hero">
                  Relay connects directly to your Aspire schedule and gives your team control over who gets notified, which services trigger a message, what the message says, and when it gets sent.
                </p>
                <div class="margin-top margin-small">
                  <div class="button-group is-center">
                    <a href={earlyAccessHref} class="button-2 w-button" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Request early access</a>
                    <a href={signInUrl} class="button-2 is-secondary w-button" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sign in</a>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="section_layout507 products-band">
  <div class="padding-global">
    <div class="container-large">
      <div class="padding-section-medium">
        <div class="products-grid">
          <article class="products-card">
            <h2 class="heading-style-h6">What it is</h2>
            <p class="text-size-medium">
              A better way to manage pre- and post-service SMS notifications using the schedule, contacts, and service data you already have in Aspire.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="products-card">
            <h2 class="heading-style-h6">Built for</h2>
            <p class="text-size-medium">
              Businesses whose clients expect proactive communication, especially high-end residential customers, plant health care and chemical application clients, and detail-oriented commercial property managers who expect advance notice.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="products-card">
            <h2 class="heading-style-h6">Works with</h2>
            <p class="text-size-medium">
              Your existing Aspire organization and Quo or Dialpad for SMS.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section_layout507">
  <div class="padding-global">
    <div class="container-large">
      <div class="padding-section-medium">
        <div class="text-align-center margin-bottom margin-medium">
          <h2 class="heading-style-h2">Why we built it</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="products-prose">
          <p class="text-size-medium">
            Aspire already has native SMS service notifications. Many companies try them, get frustrated, and eventually turn them off.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="products-grid products-grid-follow">
          <article class="products-card">
            <h3 class="heading-style-h6">Multiple services can mean multiple texts.</h3>
            <p class="text-size-medium">
              If a customer has several work tickets scheduled for the same day, Aspire sends a separate notification for each one.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="products-card">
            <h3 class="heading-style-h6">Moving a work ticket can trigger a cancellation message.</h3>
            <p class="text-size-medium">
              Reschedule on the Schedule Board and Aspire notifies the customer that the visit was cancelled. You cannot customize that message before it goes out.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="products-card">
            <h3 class="heading-style-h6">Notifications are all or nothing.</h3>
            <p class="text-size-medium">
              There is little control over which services should generate notifications. A customer may want advance notice for spray applications and mulch but not weekly mowing.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="products-prose products-grid-follow">
          <p class="text-size-medium">
            Relay was built to give your team the control Aspire’s native notifications are missing.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section_layout507 products-band">
  <div class="padding-global">
    <div class="container-large">
      <div class="padding-section-medium">
        <div class="text-align-center margin-bottom margin-medium">
          <h2 class="heading-style-h2">How it works</h2>
        </div>
        <ol class="products-steps">
          <li class="products-step">
            <h3 class="heading-style-h6">Sync your Aspire schedule.</h3>
            <p class="text-size-medium">
              Relay pulls your upcoming schedule, properties, services, and contacts directly from Aspire.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li class="products-step">
            <h3 class="heading-style-h6">Review and customize.</h3>
            <p class="text-size-medium">
              Choose which visits and contacts get notified, then use templates for different services, customers, and pre- or post-visit communication.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li class="products-step">
            <h3 class="heading-style-h6">Send or schedule.</h3>
            <p class="text-size-medium">
              Review the consolidated notification, then send it now or schedule it.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section_layout507">
  <div class="padding-global">
    <div class="container-large">
      <div class="padding-section-medium">
        <div class="text-align-center margin-bottom margin-medium">
          <h2 class="heading-style-h2">Relay is the first of several Miri plugins for Aspire</h2>
          <p class="text-size-medium products-prose">
            We spend every day in Aspire and see the same pain points across companies. The goal is focused tools that connect to the Aspire data your team already maintains.
          </p>
        </div>
        <h3 class="heading-style-h3 text-align-center margin-bottom margin-small">Coming next</h3>
        <div class="products-grid">
          <article class="products-card">
            <h3 class="heading-style-h6">Directory</h3>
            <p class="text-size-medium">
              one-off and scheduled SMS to Aspire contacts without a work ticket.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="products-card">
            <h3 class="heading-style-h6">Proposal follow ups</h3>
            <p class="text-size-medium">
              a sequence when an opportunity moves to Delivered.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="products-card">
            <h3 class="heading-style-h6">Invoice reminders</h3>
            <p class="text-size-medium">
              automated AR workflows around open and overdue Aspire invoices.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="text-align-center products-closer">
          <p class="text-size-medium">Aspire has the data. Miri helps you do more with it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
